# A value every thread reads alike, each of whose definitions is an
# unguarded shl by a constant k or and with a constant whose low k bits
# are 0, reads as 2^k times its floor over 2^k, so its or with bits
# below 2^k is an add. A guarded shl keeps another value where its guard
# is false, and a count in a register may be smaller: the or is unknown.
# A count is its unsigned 32-bit value: 0x100000007 shifts by 7. A floor
# by a divisor the 2^k neither divides nor is divided by is refused,
# where uniform(…) alone read ⌊(3·%tid.x + b)/3⌋.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/uniform_aligned.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_uniform_aligned
CHECK: warp: 4–5 sectors (ideal 4)
CHECK-SAME: [4 * %tid.x + 512 * ⌊uniform(%r3@$L__BB0_1)/128⌋ + param_0]
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_uniform_aligned_guarded
CHECK: unknown: or whose sides may both set bit 0
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_uniform_aligned_count
CHECK: unknown: or whose sides may both set bit 0
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_uniform_aligned_mask
CHECK: warp: 4–5 sectors (ideal 4)
CHECK-SAME: [4 * %tid.x + 512 * ⌊uniform(%r6@118)/128⌋ + param_0]
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_uniform_aligned_wide_count
CHECK: warp: 4–5 sectors (ideal 4)
CHECK-SAME: [4 * %tid.x + 512 * ⌊uniform(%r3@$L__BB4_1)/128⌋ + param_0]
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_shift_wide_count
CHECK: warp: 16–17 sectors (ideal 4)
CHECK-SAME: [16 * %tid.x + param_0]
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_uniform_aligned_div
CHECK: unknown: depends on ⌊uniform(%r3@$L__BB6_1)/128⌋, in a division
